source: crates/lighthouse-cli/tests/it/surface.rs
expression: "printed(dir.path(), &args)"
---
Trust this project to run the commands it names.

The programs the project names: the command checks and fixes of its own decisions, its command models, `[fix] verify` and its plugins. Trust is yours, kept in `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lighthouse/trust.toml` (default `~/.config/lighthouse/trust.toml`) for this root and the exact `lighthouse.toml`, `.lighthouse/decisions` and personal config files (`config.toml`, `.lighthouse/local.toml`) you have read; a change to any of them withdraws it. `LIGHTHOUSE_TRUST=1` trusts every project, for CI. Without trust none of them runs: a command fix is declined, a command check is unavailable and `[fix] verify` fails; the bundled checks still run.

It lists the programs it would trust and asks for confirmation on the terminal; without a terminal it refuses unless `--yes` says you have read the list.

Usage: lighthouse trust [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --config <FILE>
          The project file; the project root is then the current directory
          
          [env: LIGHTHOUSE_CONFIG=]

      --revoke
          Withdraw the trust instead

      --color <COLOR>
          Color of help and messages. `auto` honours NO_COLOR and CLICOLOR_FORCE
          
          [env: LIGHTHOUSE_COLOR=]
          [default: auto]
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

      --yes
          Trust without asking; for scripts, after reading what is listed

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
